tandem — third-party notices
============================

tandem's own code is MIT licensed (see LICENSE).

tandem does NOT ship the planners it drives. A planner's runtime is built on your machine from
a recipe that pins each source tree to an exact commit, and `tandem init` / `tandem runtime build`
fetches those trees from their upstream repositories at install time (or reads them from a
directory you provide, for an offline machine). The sources are then under their own licences,
on your machine, exactly as if you had cloned them yourself.

Read this before redistributing tandem, or before using it with the TiPToP planner commercially.


Planners tandem fetches, but does not redistribute
--------------------------------------------------
The TiPToP planner's recipe (src/tandem/planners/tiptop/recipe.py) fetches three trees. The
exact commits, and the paths trimmed from each, are recorded there; an installed runtime records
what it actually installed in <runtime>/.tandem-runtime.json.

