tandem applies two small patches of its own to the fetched TiPToP tree
(src/tandem/planners/tiptop/patches/): one lets a profile own its camera calibration file, the
other makes pyrealsense2 an optional dependency. Each patch file says what it changes and why.


What ships inside tandem
------------------------
DATAFARM checkpoints  —  src/tandem/planners/tiptop/assets/
  vae_full_v2.pt and rnd_droid.pt, the small checkpoints the cuRobo fork's VAE-manifold and
  RND-novelty costs load. They come from the hitl-tamp-vla project, whose repository is not
  public, so tandem carries them; the install copies them into the runtime where those costs
  look for them.

lerobot_v3.py  —  src/tandem/export/lerobot_v3.py
  Adapted from the tamp-vla project's LeRobot v3.0 dataset writer.


What the NVIDIA License means for you
-------------------------------------
cuRobo and cuTAMP are under NVIDIA's source-available license, not an open-source license. Two
clauses matter here:

  §3.1 Redistribution — you may redistribute the Work only under this same license, with
       a complete copy of it included and all copyright/attribution notices retained.

  §3.3 Use Limitation — "The Work and any derivative works thereof only may be used or
       intended for use non-commercially", where non-commercial means research or
       evaluation purposes only.

tandem no longer redistributes either, so §3.1 does not bind tandem's own distribution: the
wheel carries no NVIDIA code. §3.3 still binds how you USE them. **Running tandem with the TiPToP
planner is for research and evaluation use only**, because that planner runs on cuRobo and
cuTAMP. Installing it, running it, and publishing results from it are all fine. Using it in a
commercial product is not, without a separate license from NVIDIA. A planner that does not
depend on them is not affected.

If you make an offline bundle of the sources (tools/bundle.py) and pass it on, that bundle IS a
redistribution of cuRobo and cuTAMP: keep each tree's LICENSE with it, as §3.1 requires. The
bundle tool exports whole trees, so it does.


Python dependencies
-------------------
tandem's runtime dependencies (typer, rich, pydantic, ruamel.yaml, numpy, platformdirs,
tomlkit, fastapi, uvicorn, google-genai, pillow) and its optional extras (av, pyarrow,
huggingface_hub, rerun-sdk) are installed from PyPI under their own licenses and are not
redistributed here.
